    trigger: npc_near
    conditions: speaker=meera
    priority: 1
    cooldown: 60
    chance: 0.6
    once: 0
    subtitle: 1
    fx: none
    clip: {fileID: 8300000, guid: c19ad424b8fae40e1b9af451f339b8e5, type: 3}
  - id: np_mad_01
    speaker: madhav
    text: Long night, sir?
    trigger: npc_near
    conditions: speaker=madhav
    priority: 1
    cooldown: 90
    chance: 0.6
    once: 0
    subtitle: 1
    fx: none
    clip: {fileID: 8300000, guid: 8d3146f8ee3ab4356b35a9f74b7d1492, type: 3}
  - id: np_mad_02
    speaker: madhav
    text: The keys? Safe with me, always.
    trigger: npc_near
    conditions: speaker=madhav
    priority: 1
    cooldown: 90
    chance: 0.6
    once: 0
    subtitle: 1
    fx: none
    clip: {fileID: 8300000, guid: 7914b0823545c445aaf4c5c32a0958f6, type: 3}
  - id: vl_m_01
    speaker: villager_m
    text: Up early, sir?
    trigger: npc_near
    conditions: speaker=villager_m
    priority: 1
    cooldown: 30
    chance: 0.5
    once: 0
    subtitle: 1
    fx: none
    clip: {fileID: 8300000, guid: 8f24e303d2f444c459419892aacf9a93, type: 3}
  - id: vl_m_02
    speaker: villager_m
    text: The temple bell is silent tonight.
    trigger: npc_near
    conditions: speaker=villager_m
    priority: 1
    cooldown: 30
    chance: 0.5
    once: 0
    subtitle: 1
    fx: none
    clip: {fileID: 8300000, guid: c8bd9338b9715480e993b6916f72062e, type: 3}
  - id: vl_m_03
    speaker: villager_m
    text: Thieves? In Suryapur?
    trigger: npc_near
    conditions: speaker=villager_m
    priority: 1
    cooldown: 30
    chance: 0.5
    once: 0
    subtitle: 1
    fx: none
    clip: {fileID: 8300000, guid: f68202cf5b68a4f369a3d7d271eb21e9, type: 3}
  - id: vl_f_01
    speaker: villager_f
    text: You're up early, sir.
    trigger: npc_near
    conditions: speaker=villager_f
    priority: 1
    cooldown: 30
    chance: 0.5
    once: 0
    subtitle: 1
    fx: none
    clip: {fileID: 8300000, guid: 7778f2dccf9e642519a9e0206500010c, type: 3}
  - id: vl_f_02
    speaker: villager_f
    text: We are praying for the festival.
    trigger: npc_near
    conditions: speaker=villager_f
    priority: 1
    cooldown: 30
    chance: 0.5
    once: 0
    subtitle: 1
    fx: none
    clip: {fileID: 8300000, guid: d3c1fe5b3f0e649549436f34897a32c0, type: 3}
  - id: vl_f_03
    speaker: villager_f
    text: Mind the cart, sir.
    trigger: npc_near
    conditions: speaker=villager_f
    priority: 1
    cooldown: 30
    chance: 0.5
    once: 0
    subtitle: 1
    fx: none
    clip: {fileID: 8300000, guid: 857267897d59e4de8954c43b4d31a6a4, type: 3}
  - id: end_narr_01
    speaker: narrator
    text: Every temple holds a story. Every artifact carries a memory. Protecting heritage means protecting our history.
    trigger: ending
    conditions:
    priority: 5
    cooldown: 0
    chance: 1
    once: 1
    subtitle: 1
    fx: none
    clip: {fileID: 8300000, guid: 87c84e754681248ceac53af48be5a478, type: 3}
  - id: lore_ary_z1
    speaker: aryan
    text: I have recovered the bell and conch teaching replica.
    trigger: lore
    conditions:
    priority: 5
    cooldown: 0
    chance: 1
    once: 0
    subtitle: 1
    fx: none
    clip: {fileID: 8300000, guid: 9fb3e75cd30d44061a199614fbf590aa, type: 3}
  - id: lore_puj_z1_1
    speaker: pujari
    text: At Puri in Odisha, the present Shree Jagannath Temple began under King Anantavarman Chodaganga Deva of the Eastern Ganga dynasty in the twelfth century.
    trigger: lore
    conditions:
    priority: 5
    cooldown: 0
    chance: 1
    once: 0
    subtitle: 1
    fx: none
    clip: {fileID: 8300000, guid: 7c19c842c098e4ca7b77adb69e30f26a, type: 3}
  - id: lore_puj_z1_2
    speaker: pujari
    text: This bell and conch recall Mangal Aarti, the early morning worship of Jagannath. Their sound calls attention to prayer and the daily service that keeps the temple tradition alive.
    trigger: lore
    conditions:
    priority: 5
    cooldown: 0
    chance: 1
    once: 0
    subtitle: 1
    fx: none
    clip: {fileID: 8300000, guid: f243626234ab1406d92ef0e7e0c16155, type: 3}
  - id: lore_puj_z1_3
    speaker: pujari
    text: Temple tradition also tells of King Indradyumna and sacred timber. That is a cherished foundation legend, distinct from the documented history of the present stone temple.
    trigger: lore
    conditions:
    priority: 5
    cooldown: 0
    chance: 1
    once: 0
    subtitle: 1
    fx: none
    clip: {fileID: 8300000, guid: 9ef646d0ca50443f79dcf0c92eba85c4, type: 3}
  - id: lore_puj_z1_extra
    speaker: pujari
    text: Legends express devotion and community identity. Historical claims use inscriptions and other evidence; both deserve careful explanation.
    trigger: lore
    conditions:
    priority: 5
    cooldown: 0
    chance: 1
    once: 0
    subtitle: 1
    fx: none
    clip: {fileID: 8300000, guid: ec018fe4b91714f27b3e49db192ae3dd, type: 3}
  - id: lore_ary_z2
    speaker: aryan
    text: I have recovered the palm-leaf teaching manuscript.
    trigger: lore
    conditions:
    priority: 5
    cooldown: 0
    chance: 1
    once: 0
    subtitle: 1
    fx: none
    clip: {fileID: 8300000, guid: 71795b3d4b5944890b3d83e09108520c, type: 3}
  - id: lore_puj_z2_1
    speaker: pujari
    text: This palm-leaf manuscript recalls tala patra, an Odisha craft that preserves writing and pictures on prepared palm leaves. Artists incise fine lines with a stylus and darken them with pigment.
    trigger: lore
    conditions:
    priority: 5
    cooldown: 0
    chance: 1
    once: 0
    subtitle: 1
    fx: none
    clip: {fileID: 8300000, guid: ac91f750bf5d44dccbc773602c63895f, type: 3}
  - id: lore_puj_z2_2
    speaker: pujari
    text: The Gita Govinda was composed by the twelfth-century poet Jayadeva. Its devotional verses are sung in Jagannath worship, connecting poetry, music and temple service.
    trigger: lore
    conditions:
    priority: 5
    cooldown: 0
    chance: 1
    once: 0
    subtitle: 1
    fx: none
    clip: {fileID: 8300000, guid: fe5184518584e4673b8804d2319b345c, type: 3}
  - id: lore_puj_z2_3
    speaker: pujari
    text: Preserving a manuscript protects more than words. It keeps a language, an artist's skill and generations of community memory available to the people who come after us.
    trigger: lore
    conditions:
    priority: 5
    cooldown: 0
    chance: 1
    once: 0
    subtitle: 1
    fx: none
    clip: {fileID: 8300000, guid: d3a05abcd375e425ba622d177f02a00b, type: 3}
  - id: lore_puj_z2_extra
    speaker: pujari
    text: Manuscripts preserve language, poetry and the knowledge of their makers. Real leaves are fragile and need trained conservation rather than a quick repair.
    trigger: lore
    conditions:
    priority: 5
    cooldown: 0
    chance: 1
    once: 0
    subtitle: 1
    fx: none
    clip: {fileID: 8300000, guid: 4906191e51d4d4bc7bb2af1397a6f99c, type: 3}
  - id: lore_ary_z3
    speaker: aryan
    text: I have recovered the wheel seal and painted teaching medallion.
    trigger: lore
    conditions:
    priority: 5
    cooldown: 0
    chance: 1
    once: 0
    subtitle: 1
    fx: none
    clip: {fileID: 8300000, guid: 7030b1d6bf66a4710a723fda8ee65784, type: 3}
  - id: lore_puj_z3_1
    speaker: pujari
    text: The Nilachakra is the sacred wheel above the Shree Jagannath Temple at Puri. It is made from ashtadhatu, an alloy traditionally described as eight metals.
    trigger: lore
    conditions:
    priority: 5
    cooldown: 0
    chance: 1
    once: 0
    subtitle: 1
    fx: none
    clip: {fileID: 8300000, guid: ebc2ce3faa6cb4d04a918afd4bfd7f43, type: 3}
  - id: lore_puj_z3_2
    speaker: pujari
    text: The temple flag is associated with this wheel. The small seal you recovered recalls that landmark; the actual sacred wheel remains on the temple.
    trigger: lore
    conditions:
    priority: 5
    cooldown: 0
    chance: 1
    once: 0
    subtitle: 1
    fx: none
    clip: {fileID: 8300000, guid: 78bd7f3b5ad5a4a95929ac097cc4f009, type: 3}
  - id: lore_puj_z3_3
    speaker: pujari
    text: Pattachitra is Odisha's detailed story-painting tradition. Artists use careful outlines and prepared colours to preserve devotional stories, including stories associated with Jagannath.
    trigger: lore
    conditions:
    priority: 5
    cooldown: 0
    chance: 1
    once: 0
    subtitle: 1
    fx: none
    clip: {fileID: 8300000, guid: aff8821621e4d4de2b03c85b2265325a, type: 3}
  - id: lore_puj_z3_extra
    speaker: pujari
    text: Pattachitra carries stories through line, colour and patient workshop practice. Supporting practising artists helps skills pass between generations.
    trigger: lore
    conditions:
    priority: 5
    cooldown: 0
    chance: 1
    once: 0
    subtitle: 1
    fx: none
    clip: {fileID: 8300000, guid: 23080be8741b545298311489812499dd, type: 3}
  - id: lore_ary_z4
    speaker: aryan
    text: I have recovered the ceremonial teaching vessel.
    trigger: lore
    conditions:
    priority: 5
    cooldown: 0
    chance: 1
    once: 0
    subtitle: 1
    fx: none
    clip: {fileID: 8300000, guid: b2ec5ceb31f0e40128e868aee232eeab, type: 3}
  - id: lore_puj_z4_1
    speaker: pujari
    text: This vessel introduces Mahaprasad, the sacred food offered at Shree Jagannath Temple. The temple kitchen prepares offerings in earthen pots through the skilled service of its cooks.
    trigger: lore
    conditions:
    priority: 5
    cooldown: 0
    chance: 1
    once: 0
    subtitle: 1
    fx: none
    clip: {fileID: 8300000, guid: 71d75e553f2924a48a20db7536e6e159, type: 3}
  - id: lore_puj_z4_2
    speaker: pujari
    text: Rohini Kunda is a sacred water place within the temple tradition. A water vessel can help us remember the place of water, offerings and daily care in worship.
    trigger: lore
    conditions:
    priority: 5
    cooldown: 0
    chance: 1
    once: 0
    subtitle: 1
    fx: none
    clip: {fileID: 8300000, guid: e468d2933f17a4a0d903ed84dbfb13bb, type: 3}
  - id: lore_puj_z4_3
    speaker: pujari
    text: Nirmalya includes dried sacred rice cherished by devotees. Food traditions remind us that heritage lives through people who prepare, share and care for it, as well as through buildings.
    trigger: lore
    conditions:
    priority: 5
    cooldown: 0
    chance: 1
    once: 0
    subtitle: 1
    fx: none
    clip: {fileID: 8300000, guid: bed30315383f648c08ea87337b9b33d3, type: 3}
  - id: lore_puj_z4_extra
    speaker: pujari
    text: Living heritage includes the people who maintain a tradition. We honour their knowledge and work, and avoid treating sacred food as treasure or a commodity.
    trigger: lore
    conditions:
    priority: 5
    cooldown: 0
    chance: 1
    once: 0
    subtitle: 1
    fx: none
    clip: {fileID: 8300000, guid: 6d5541474031a49b295ff08fde3d26d9, type: 3}
  - id: lore_ary_z5
    speaker: aryan
    text: I have recovered the chariot teaching medallion and banner.
    trigger: lore
    conditions:
    priority: 5
    cooldown: 0
    chance: 1
    once: 0
    subtitle: 1
    fx: none
    clip: {fileID: 8300000, guid: d706322aaa88b4d368605ac3f469de39, type: 3}
  - id: lore_puj_z5_1
    speaker: pujari
    text: Ratha Yatra is the great chariot festival of Puri. Jagannath, Balabhadra and Subhadra travel along Bada Danda, the Grand Avenue, towards Gundicha Temple.
    trigger: lore
    conditions:
    priority: 5
    cooldown: 0
    chance: 1
    once: 0
    subtitle: 1
    fx: none
    clip: {fileID: 8300000, guid: a4255cbd3236746738b62b2ef523b700, type: 3}
  - id: lore_puj_z5_2
    speaker: pujari
    text: Jagannath's chariot is Nandighosha, with sixteen wheels. Balabhadra's is Taladhwaja and Subhadra's is Darpadalana. Each chariot has its own established design.
    trigger: lore
    conditions:
    priority: 5
    cooldown: 0
    chance: 1
    once: 0
    subtitle: 1
    fx: none
    clip: {fileID: 8300000, guid: 0cfc03965d0b547ffbb752f16a4ab32d, type: 3}
  - id: lore_puj_z5_3
    speaker: pujari
    text: Skilled carpenters build the chariots anew each year. The wheel and banner recall a living tradition in which making, devotion and community participation carry knowledge forward.
    trigger: lore
    conditions:
    priority: 5
    cooldown: 0
    chance: 1
    once: 0
    subtitle: 1
    fx: none
    clip: {fileID: 8300000, guid: 9081f778799e84742b2c8ed230452e91, type: 3}
  - id: lore_puj_z5_extra
    speaker: pujari
    text: Rebuilding keeps specialist skills alive through practice and transmission. The knowledge of the makers matters as much as the finished woodwork.
    trigger: lore
    conditions:
    priority: 5
    cooldown: 0
    chance: 1
    once: 0
    subtitle: 1
    fx: none
    clip: {fileID: 8300000, guid: a78c71d262ad54b438a46eb5fd142ab2, type: 3}
  - id: lore_ary_z6
    speaker: aryan
    text: I have recovered the teaching finial and chronicle ornament.
    trigger: lore
    conditions:
    priority: 5
    cooldown: 0
    chance: 1
    once: 0
    subtitle: 1
    fx: none
    clip: {fileID: 8300000, guid: b200d56ee46724c78949b719d96754f6, type: 3}
  - id: lore_puj_z6_1
    speaker: pujari
    text: A kalasha is a crowning vessel form in temple architecture. This finial ornament helps us notice how the upper parts of a temple contribute to its identity and craftsmanship.
    trigger: lore
    conditions:
    priority: 5
    cooldown: 0
    chance: 1
    once: 0
    subtitle: 1
    fx: none
    clip: {fileID: 8300000, guid: edd962e53458648019819a2e8556a283, type: 3}
  - id: lore_puj_z6_2
    speaker: pujari
    text: At Puri, Nabakalebara is the periodic renewal of the sacred wooden images in the Jagannath tradition. The images are associated with sacred neem wood, or daru.
    trigger: lore
    conditions:
    priority: 5
    cooldown: 0
    chance: 1
    once: 0
    subtitle: 1
    fx: none
    clip: {fileID: 8300000, guid: 78ad8a813a2bc4a64806c5315ede2593, type: 3}
  - id: lore_puj_z6_3
    speaker: pujari
    text: This is why heritage is more than the price of wood or metal. People preserve and renew its meaning through knowledge, care and worship. Protecting heritage means protecting living community memory.
    trigger: lore
    conditions:
    priority: 5
    cooldown: 0
    chance: 1
    once: 0
    subtitle: 1
    fx: none
    clip: {fileID: 8300000, guid: b4cfef74c64414b5aa8047f40f15bf43, type: 3}
  - id: lore_puj_z6_extra
    speaker: pujari
    text: People renew heritage through knowledge, care and shared responsibility. Every temple holds a story; protecting heritage means protecting our history.
    trigger: lore
    conditions:
    priority: 5
    cooldown: 0
    chance: 1
    once: 0
    subtitle: 1
    fx: none
    clip: {fileID: 8300000, guid: b07a7edfbbc0946ccbe9f0b92271a0aa, type: 3}
  - id: lore_skip_01
    speaker: aryan
    text: Moving ahead to the next lead.
    trigger: lore
    conditions:
    priority: 5
    cooldown: 0
    chance: 1
    once: 0
    subtitle: 1
    fx: none
    clip: {fileID: 8300000, guid: 46953e6b323684b77af14c5353167596, type: 3}
  - id: lore_return_01
    speaker: pujari
    text: Bring every teaching piece to the temple steps, Aryan.
    trigger: lore
    conditions:
    priority: 5
    cooldown: 0
    chance: 1
    once: 0
    subtitle: 1
    fx: none
    clip: {fileID: 8300000, guid: 3df443327b8e345ff944e64eb9e7eaef, type: 3}
  - id: lore_puj_z1_care
    speaker: pujari
    text: Keep replicas documented and handle them carefully. Real sacred objects remain in the care of their community.
    trigger: lore
    conditions:
    priority: 5
    cooldown: 0
    chance: 1
    once: 0
    subtitle: 1
    fx: none
    clip: {fileID: 8300000, guid: e37a85e2b7da84d8b8564c0bb0181f18, type: 3}
